// HISTORICAL FORMAT LINEAGES (language guide chapter 22).
//
// Published eras are ordinary immutable data declarations. A package groups
// conversion edges by supplying a nominal `Lineage` marker and explicitly
// binding each checked machine to this requirement. The marker keeps disk,
// network, cache, and snapshot histories distinct even when they happen to use
// the same `Old` and `New` carriers.
//
// The requirement intentionally does not imply reversibility. A downgrade is
// a separate edge, and a fallible package may expose a result sum of its own as
// the `New` carrier.
public trait FormatMigration<Lineage, Old, New> {
    machine migrate(old: Old, out: &mut New);
}
